Source: the rust-iouring-kensac submission by @kensac (PR #264) to
https://github.com/arjaythedev/twelve-dollar-server-challenge (MIT). Its files are copied
unmodified into datasources/reference/; datasources/csrc/shim.c is a copy with one #ifdef __linux__ guard.
SQLite is public domain; the pinned 3.54.1 amalgamation is fetched by deploy/scripts/fetch-sqlite.sh
(not committed). datasources/csrc/lean_glue.c carries an fcntl64 stub for Lean's older bundled glibc.

datasources/store/ is a subtree of V-Sekai-fire's store repository (SQLite with a FoundationDB VFS), licensed
under either Apache-2.0 (datasources/store/LICENSE-APACHE) or MIT (datasources/store/LICENSE-MIT). libweftfdb builds from it
but no executable links it yet.

datasources/hargup/ is the lean-derive-hargup submission by Harsh Gupta (@hargup, PR #153) to
https://github.com/arjaythedev/twelve-dollar-server-challenge (MIT, copyright arjaythedev and the challenge
contributors; the licence is copied beside it), at commit 39cd79b2a2ce9e01f99352c1fe8209cb2afc80c1. Its files are
copied from that commit; the only changes are CITATION.cff, LICENSE, and the fatal-error path (commit "Route every fatal
runtime error through rt_fatal": exit() and abort() became rt_fatal in runtime/*.c, defined in runtime/rt.h). The challenge's README says a
submission is licensed under the repository's MIT licence. SQLite is fetched by its build.sh with a pinned SHA-256.
